<title>USA: Wal-Mart plans to double shr buyback.</title>
<headline>Wal-Mart plans to double shr buyback.</headline>
<dateline>BENTONVILLE, Ark. 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wal-Mart Stores Inc said Friday it plans to double its share repurchase program, raising the total authorization to $400 million.</p>
<p>The company said it has acquired about $181 million in stock under this program.</p>
<p>Purchases will be made from time to time in the open market and shares will be used in the company's stock option and other benefit plans, the company said.</p>
<p>The shares repurchased represent less than 1 percent of the approximately 2.3 billion shares outstanding, the company said.</p>
</text>
